omments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-best-way-to-read-a-book-that-nobody-s-doing--b4q6ahals","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/zIqLuuyxgE4/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-20T20:33:42.000Z"},{"id":"xOdbOfJoj","title":"How to Actually Understand Dense Machine Learning Papers - Solveit free lesson","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U5akUYqCqnA","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-actually-understand-dense-machine-learning-papers---solveit-free-lesson-xodbofjoj","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/U5akUYqCqnA/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-20T20:33:42.000Z"},{"id":"sijaoK0AC","title":"Build to Last \u2014 Chris Latter talks with Jeremy Howard","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WJS2YDZO-vc","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/build-to-last-chris-latter-talks-with-jeremy-howard-sijaok0ac","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/WJS2YDZO-vc/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-10-30T21:01:45.000Z"},{"id":"rsfUnZfrg","title":"A Rapid Tour of the Solveit Platform","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bxDDLMe6KuU","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/a-rapid-tour-of-the-solveit-platform-rsfunzfrg","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bxDDLMe6KuU/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-10-17T22:05:35.000Z"},{"id":"e9i1Ek1Wv","title":"What is Solveit? Showing some recent use cases","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m-GOZSi2R_Q","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-is-solveit-showing-some-recent-use-cases-e9i1ek1wv","summary":"Solveit is a Jupyter-style interactive coding environment that combines live code execution with AI assistance. It enables iterative, exploratory programming where developers can write code, execute it in real-time, and get AI help when needed. Use cases include web scraping, ML model exploration, data analysis, and mathematical problem-solving. The tool emphasizes human-AI collaboration rather than full automation, allowing developers to maintain control while leveraging AI for specific tasks like writing plotting code, regular expressions, or explaining concepts.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/m-GOZSi2R_Q/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-10-03T05:49:18.000Z"},{"id":"llen9jiKj","title":"Sarah Pan, teenage AI wizard","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LDklFaxssFE","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sarah-pan-teenage-ai-wizard-llen9jikj","summary":"Sarah Pan, a high school student, achieved significant recognition by being published in NERPS, a premier academic AI conference. Her research focused on improving large language models' ability to perform logical reasoning and mathematical calculations. She collaborated with renowned experts, and her journey highlights the potential for young students to excel in advanced AI research through online courses and dedicated self-study. Sarah also discusses her experiences at MIT and her ongoing work at Answer AI.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/LDklFaxssFE/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-03-18T19:08:36.000Z"},{"id":"jljYth6rV","title":"Build Python web apps quickly with MonsterUI","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EtZ4pEzPMcc","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/monsterui-beautiful-python-web-apps-in-minutes-jljyth6rv","summary":"MonsterUI is a Python library that enables developers to build beautiful web apps quickly and efficiently with minimal CSS and JavaScript knowledge. It leverages fast HTML and integrates with Tailwind CSS for a smooth development experience. The library builds on top of frameworks like Franken UI and Shaden, providing sensible defaults and easy-to-use components. MonsterUI is designed to streamline the process of creating production-ready web apps, making it accessible even for those without advanced design skills.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/EtZ4pEzPMcc/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-11T20:13:34.000Z"},{"id":"tGrBGVzSg","title":"How To Solve It With Code\u2014background on the course; a discussion with Jeremy and Hamel","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e9tL_Eg3fpM","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-solve-it-with-code-background-on-the-course-a-discussion-with-jeremy-and-hamel-tgrbgvzsg","summary":"Jeremy and Hamel discuss the evolution and vision behind Fast AI, emphasizing its role in making AI accessible to a wider audience. They introduce a new course, 'How to Solve It With Code,' which integrates AI into the learning process, offering a more interactive and iterative approach with the concept of dialogue engineering. This method aims to combine human and AI strengths to tackle complex problems more effectively, enhancing both the learning experience and practical application of AI in coding.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/e9tL_Eg3fpM/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-11-07T22:58:52.000Z"},{"id":"eEEiNPPNR","title":"How To Solve It With Code \u2014 Overview","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YKeXxj4geRo","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-solve-it-with-code-overview-eeeinppnr","summary":"Fast AI is launching a new course designed to teach coding with the aid of AI language models. The course aims to help programmers avoid the pitfalls of generating large, unmanageable code by building coding skills gradually and iteratively. Targeted at those with basic Python knowledge but no computer science degree, it offers hands-on learning with a custom tool, live sessions, and collaborative learning. This beta course is designed to evolve with participant feedback to create a comprehensive learning experience.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/YKeXxj4geRo/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-11-07T22:57:07.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["youtube","portalrunner","goto","developervoices","ndc"],"opposite_handles":["horde","dailydevworld","watercooler","on_leuwcq","devtools"],"similar":[{"id":"youtube","handle":"youtube","name":"YouTube","is_squad":false,"x":-4.7734,"y":-10.2627,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":872,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--W5zMumpP--/f_auto/v1725350181/logos/youtube","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":9.762112,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.021216,"avg_read_time":38.279817,"tag_diversity":0.455275},"top_tags_preview":[["ai",143],["python",75],["machine-learning",61]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[4.8529,2.4853],"cadence_depth":[9.6765,9.6176],"hype_variety":[4.9853,9.8676],"title_style":[-0.7353,4.5294]}},{"id":"portalrunner","handle":"portalrunner","name":"PortalRunner","is_squad":false,"x":-4.7303,"y":-10.1143,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":54,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--aSL1WXXp--/f_auto/v1756381503/logos/portalrunner","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":1.503921,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":52.981481,"tag_diversity":0.351852},"top_tags_preview":[["hardware",2],["signal-processing",2],["javascript",2]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[2.5735,8.4265],"cadence_depth":[-4.0,9.7353],"hype_variety":[-5.7941,-3.2206],"title_style":[7.7353,-3.2794]}},{"id":"goto","handle":"goto","name":"GOTO Conferences","is_squad":false,"x":-4.9443,"y":-10.4915,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":457,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--rax7fnoD--/f_auto/v1704628081/logos/goto.jpg","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":3.785949,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.105033,"avg_read_time":34.185996,"tag_diversity":0.568928},"top_tags_preview":[["architecture",73],["devops",61],["ai",54]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-5.8235,-3.6324],"cadence_depth":[8.1765,9.5147],"hype_variet